# Otonom Media — product north star

Canonical intent for humans and agents working in this repo. Do not drift into rebuilding HeyGen Video Agent locally.

## Primary goal (personal ops → later product)

Replace **OpusClip.pro** + manual **NotebookLM → caption → multi-platform publish** so the operator can focus on client work (~$17/hr), not glue work between tools.

**Closed loop that must exist** (otherwise HeyGen/Creator alone does not solve the pain):

```text
topic / source
  → generate or import long-form (HeyGen VA / NotebookLM / YouTube)
  → land in Review (one approve inbox)
  → schedule + publish (YouTube / Shorts / TikTok / Telegram / …)
  → optional: auto-clip long-form → more shorts
```

Human review before publish is intentional. Automate everything *except* that approve step.

## Content types (one dashboard eventually)

Not video-only. Same platform should eventually handle:

| Type | Sources / references | Role of this repo |
|------|----------------------|-------------------|
| Video long-form | HeyGen Creator Video Agent (preferred quality); import URL/file | Orchestrate + Review + distribute — **do not** rebuild VA visuals in FFmpeg |
| Video shorts | Existing clip factory (OpusClip replacement) | Core — harden first |
| Text + image posts | `techtalk-autonomous`; better text patterns from `sahibul-nf/social-media-content-ai-generation` | Unify into dashboard later; improve prompts, don’t fork a second video stack |

## Cost / HeyGen rules of thumb

- **Creator ($29/mo) premium credits** ≠ **Direct API wallet (USD)**. MCP/OAuth uses Creator credits; app `X-Api-Key` uses API wallet.
- Avatar group / looks / cloned voices created on Creator are **assets on the account** — reusable via API with the same IDs; you still **pay API usage** separately when calling Direct API.
- Prefer: HeyGen as long-form **engine**; this app as **distribution + review + shorts**.

## Priority order (when choosing work)

1. Clip → Review → schedule → publish reliability (OpusClip replacement)
2. Path A: HeyGen MCP (Creator) → `ingest_longform` → Review → schedule (`docs/heygen-paths.md`)
3. Optional: Path B Direct API when Creator exhausted / no Cursor (`heygen_client.py`)
4. Unify text/image post flows into the same dashboard
5. Defer: Virtuals Protocol / A2A until Web2 loop runs weekly without babysitting
6. Do **not**: chase FFmpeg/HyperFrames parity with Video Agent Quality Mode

